==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
From {{der|eo|it|si}}, {{der|eo|fr|soi}}, {{der|eo|es|se}}, {{der|eo|la|se}}, plus the ''i'' of personal pronouns.

===Pronunciation===
{{eo-pr|a=Eo-si.ogg;LL-Q143 (epo)-Lepticed7-si.wav;LL-Q143 (epo)-Robin van der Vliet-si.wav}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|eo|pronouns|reflexive||accusative|sin|possessive|sia}}

# [[himself]], [[herself]], [[itself]], [[themselves]], [[oneself]]

====Usage notes====
The reflexive pronoun ''si'' is only used to refer to the third person (In English: [[he]]/[[she]]/[[it]]/[[they]]) not the first or second person (In English: [[I]]/[[we]]/[[you]]). When the subject of a sentence is first or second person, the same pronoun is repeated (with the accusative ending {{m|eo|-n}} added if needed) instead of using ''si''. (E.g. "they wash '''themselves'''" is ''ili lavas '''sin''''', but "I wash '''myself'''" is ''mi lavas '''min''''', instead of *''mi lavas sin''.)

===See also===
