====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|it|-si||enclitic}}
* {{alt|it|se||before an accusative particle, or [[ne]]}}
* {{alt|it|ci||before another [[si]]}}

====Pronunciation====
{{it-pr|si̇°<r:DiPI<<name:dipi>>>,si̇<r:DOP:lid#1082792><audio:It-si.ogg><rhyme:->}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|it|pronouns}}

# {{senseid|it|reflexive}} {{lb|it|reflexive pronoun}} [[oneself]], [[himself]], [[herself]], [[itself]], [[themselves]]
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Il tuo gatto '''si''' lava sul mio letto.|Your cat cleans '''himself'''/'''itself''' on my bed.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|La tua gatta '''si''' lava sul mio letto.|Your cat cleans '''herself''' on my bed.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Marco '''si''' è rotto il braccio.|Marco has broken '''his''' arm.}}
# {{senseid|it|reciprocal}} {{lb|it|reciprocal pronoun}} [[each other]], [[one another]]
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Carlo e Laura '''si''' amano.|Carlo and Laura love '''each other'''.}}
# {{senseid|it|indefinite}} {{lb|it|indefinite}} [[one]], [[you]], [[we]], [[they]], [[people]]
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|In Italia '''si''' pranza intorno all'una.|In Italy '''they''' eat lunch around 13.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|In Italia '''si''' tende ad andare a letto tardi.|In Italy, '''people''' tend to go to bed late.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|'''Si''' dice che Maria volesse uccidere Giovanni.|'''It is''' said that Maria wanted to kill Giovanni.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Da questa finestra '''si''' vede la banca.|From this window, '''one''' can see the bank.}}
# {{senseid|it|passive}} {{lb|it|si passivante}} {{n-g|Used to form the [[passive voice]] of a verb}}; [[it]]
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|'''Si''' vende latte.'' / ''Vende'''si''' latte.|Milk for sale.}}
#: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Non '''si''' accettano carte di credito.|Credit cards are not accepted.}}
# {{senseid|it|first person}} {{lb|it|dialectal|notably|_|Rome}} {{n-g|reflexive and reciprocal first person pronoun, where Standard Italian uses {{m|it|ci}}}}
#: {{uxa|it|'''Se''' semo fatti sei chilometri [[a fette]].|q=[[farsi|'''Ci''' siamo fatti]] sei chilometri [[a piedi]].|We walked for six kilometers.}}
#: {{uxa|it|Volemo'''se''' bene.|q=Vogliamo'''ci''' bene.|Let's love each other.}}
#: {{uxa|it|'''Se''' la [[smezzare|smezzamo]]?|q='''Ce''' la dividiamo?|Do you want to split?}}
#* {{quote-book|it|author=Matteo Maria Boiardo|title=Orlando Innamorato|year=1483|section=I, XVIII|lines=37–39|text=Ambo '''se''' poseremo in questo prato <br> e domatina, come il giorno pare, <br> ritornaremo insieme a battagliare.|t=We will both lie down in this meadow <br> and tomorrow morning, when the day appears, <br> together we will go back to fight.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When {{m|it|si}} is part of an infinitive, it can be placed before it as a separate word, but more often it is attached to the end. In this case, the final -''e'' of the infinitive is dropped, or, in the case of infinitives ending in -''rre'', the final -''re'' is dropped. Examples: {{m|it|amare|amar(e)}} + {{m|it|si}} = {{m|it|amarsi}}; {{m|it|ridurre|ridur(re)}} + {{m|it|si}} = {{m|it|ridursi}}.
* Often translated using the passive voice in English when used as indefinite personal pronoun:
*: {{uxa|it|Si dice che {{...}}|It is said that {{...}}}}
* ''Verb'' + {{m|it|si}} is often translated as {{m|en|become}} or {{m|en|get}} + [past participle] in English.
* In cases where {{m|it|si|pos=indefinite pronoun}} and {{m|it|si|pos=reflexive pronoun}} follow each other, the first {{m|it|si}} is replaced with {{m|it|ci}}:
*: {{uxa|inline=1|it|Ci si lava.|One washes oneself.}}
*: (instead of: ''{{lang|it|*Si si lava.}}'')
* Becomes {{m|it|se}} when followed by a third-person direct object clitic ({{m|it|lo}}, {{m|it|la}}, {{m|it|li}}, {{m|it|le}}, or {{m|it|ne}}).

