===Etymology 1===
{{root|nb|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=say}}
{{inh+|nb|gmq-mno|segia|t=to say}},<ref>Endre Mørck (2015), “[https://ojs.novus.no/index.php/MOM/article/download/1209/1198 Hovedtrekk ved akkusativ med infinitiv i mellomnorsk]”, in ''Maal og Minne'', number 2, pages 43–85, here page 60, example 24a, citing ''Diplomatarium Norvegicum'' I, number 657 (1418).</ref> from {{inh|nb|non|segja}}, from {{inh|nb|gem-pro|*sagjaną}}, ultimately from {{der|nb|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|id=say|t=to say}}.

Compare {{cog|nn|seia}}, {{cog|da|sige}}, {{cog|sv|säga}}, {{cog|is|segja}}, {{cog|fo|siga}}, {{cog|de|sagen}} and {{cog|en|say|t=to say}}.

====Verb====
{{head|nb|verb|imperative|si|present tense|sier|passive|sies|simple past|sa|supine|sagt|past participle|sagt|present participle|siende|verbal noun|siing}}

# To [[say]], to [[utter]].
#: {{uxi|nb|«Jeg kommer snart», '''sa''' hun.|“I'll come soon,” she '''said'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879|author=P. Chr. Asbjørnsen|title=Norske Folke- og Huldre-Eventyr|page=25|passage=«Jeg er ikke ræd for trold og trugsmaal», '''sagde''' gutten|translation=“I am not afraid of trolls and threats,” '''said''' the boy.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1882|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=En folkefiende|page=161|passage=når har jeg '''sagt''' det på tryk?|translation=When have I '''said''' that in print?}}
#: '''som sagt''' — “as already mentioned”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|'''Som sagt''' begynner møtet klokka tre.|'''As already mentioned''', the meeting starts at three.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1881|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Gengangere|page=72|passage=jeg er jo, som '''sagt''', ikke inde i den slags ting|translation=As I have '''said''', I am not familiar with that sort of thing.}}
#: '''som sagt, så gjort''' — “no sooner said than done”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|Vi bestemte oss for å reise. '''Som sagt, så gjort'''.|We decided to leave. '''No sooner said than done'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson|title=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnsons fortællinger|page=238|passage=hver kunde kjøbe det, han vilde, og dele udbyttet. Som '''sagt''', så gjort|translation=Each could buy what he wanted and share the proceeds. No sooner '''said''' than done.}}
#: '''lettere sagt enn gjort''' — “easier said than done”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|Å endre gamle vaner er '''lettere sagt enn gjort'''.|Changing old habits is '''easier said than done'''.}}
#: '''si etter''' — “to repeat after; quote”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|'''Si etter''' meg: «Jeg lover å prøve.»|'''Repeat after''' me: “I promise to try.”}}
#: '''for å si det med''' — “to quote; in the words of”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|'''For å si det med''' læreren vår: «Øvelse gjør mester.»|'''To quote''' our teacher: “Practice makes perfect.”}}
#: '''si ja og amen''' — “to agree unquestioningly”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|Du trenger ikke å '''si ja og amen''' til alt.|You don't have to '''agree unquestioningly''' to everything.}}
#: '''har man sagt a, får man si b''' — “in for a penny, in for a pound; having started, one must follow through”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|Nå har vi begynt, og '''har man sagt a, får man si b'''.|We've started now, and '''in for a penny, in for a pound'''.}}
## To [[say]] a greeting, farewell, thanks, or similar conventional expression.
##: {{uxi|nb|Hun '''sa''' god natt til barna.|She '''said''' goodnight to the children.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1888|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Fruen fra havet|page=48|passage=[jeg] får nok '''sige''' tak for mig|translation=[I] had better '''say''' my thanks and goodbye.}}
## To [[pronounce]] a word in a particular way or use a particular grammatical form.<ref>''Det Norske Akademis ordbok'', “si”, verb, sense 1.2.</ref>
##: {{uxi|nb|Hun '''sier''' «kjerke» der jeg '''sier''' «kirke».|She '''says''' “kjerke” where I '''say''' “kirke”.}}
## To [[use]] a particular word, expression, or form of address.
##: {{uxi|nb|Du kan '''si''' du til meg.|You can '''address''' me as ''du''.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1881|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Gengangere|page=142|passage=hvorfor kan du ikke '''sige''' du til mig, Regine?|translation=Why can't you '''address''' me with the familiar “du”, Regine?}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1884|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Vildanden|page=59|passage=krøllet vil jeg ikke egentlig kalde det [håret]; jeg vil snarere '''sige''' lokket|translation=I would not really call it [the hair] curly; I would rather '''say''' wavy.}}
##: '''for ikke å si''' — “not to say; if not”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Rommet var lite, '''for ikke å si''' trangt.|The room was small, '''not to say''' cramped.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1930|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Samlede verker|volume=XV|page=313|passage=[gudshuset] staar paa svage for ikke at '''sige''' faldefærdige fødder|translation=[The church] stands on weak—not to '''say''' crumbling—foundations.}}
## To [[express]], to [[put into words]].
##: {{uxi|nb|Jeg kan ikke '''si''' hvor glad jeg er.|I cannot '''express''' how happy I am.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1882|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=En folkefiende|page=58|passage=jeg kan ikke '''sige''' Dem, kære herr Aslaksen, hvor inderligt det glæder mig|translation=I cannot '''tell''' you, dear Mr Aslaksen, how deeply this delights me.}}
## To [[put]], to [[phrase]]; to express in a specified manner.
##: {{uxi|nb|Kan du '''si''' det på en enklere måte?|Can you '''put''' it more simply?}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1884|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Vildanden|page=159|passage='''sig''' det bent ud, Ekdal!|translation='''Say''' it outright, Ekdal!}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1957|author=Edvard Grieg|title=Artikler og taler|page=82|passage=når jeg '''siger''', at jeg ikke blev skuffet, så er det, om muligt, endog for lidt '''sagt'''|translation=When I '''say''' that I was not disappointed, that is, if anything, an understatement.}}
##: '''for å si det sånn''' — “to put it that way”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Det gikk ikke helt etter planen, '''for å si det sånn'''.|It didn't quite go according to plan, '''to put it that way'''.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1997|author=Torgrim Eggen|title=Den nye Dylan|page=35|passage=[…] for å '''si''' det sånn|translation=[…] to '''put''' it that way}}
##: '''så å si''' — “so to speak; virtually”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Salen var '''så å si''' full.|The hall was '''virtually''' full.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1874|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Peer Gynt|page=150|passage=det hele er, så at '''sige''', privat|translation=The whole thing is, so to '''speak''', private.}}
##: '''snart sagt''' {{q|now rare}} — “practically; almost”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Han kjente '''snart sagt''' alle i byen.|He knew '''practically''' everyone in town.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1909|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Efterladte Skrifter|volume=I|page=318|passage=disse kendsgerninger kunde suppleres snart '''sagt''' i det uendelige|translation=These facts could be supplemented virtually without end.}}
##: '''om jeg så må si''' — “if I may put it that way”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Han var festens midtpunkt, '''om jeg så må si'''.|He was the centre of the party, '''if I may put it that way'''.}}
##: '''med permisjon å si''' {{q|dated}} — “if I may say so; pardon the expression”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Dette er, '''med permisjon å si''', tull.|This is, '''if I may say so''', nonsense.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1874|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=De unges forbund|page=208|passage=[madam Rundholmen] så ud som en havfrue, med permission at '''sige'''|translation=[Madam Rundholmen] looked like a mermaid, if I may '''say''' so.}}
##: '''kort sagt''' — “in short”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|'''Kort sagt''' trenger vi mer tid.|'''In short''', we need more time.}}
##: '''nær sagt''' — “one might almost say”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Vi har ventet i, '''nær sagt''', en evighet.|We have waited for, '''one might almost say''', an eternity.}}
##: '''rettere sagt''' — “or rather; more precisely”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Vi møtes i morgen, eller '''rettere sagt''' i kveld.|We'll meet tomorrow, '''or rather''' this evening.}}
##: '''sant å si''' — “to tell the truth”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|'''Sant å si''' husker jeg ikke navnet.|'''To tell the truth''', I don't remember the name.}}
##: '''for sterkt sagt''' — “put too strongly; an overstatement”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Å kalle det en katastrofe er '''for sterkt sagt'''.|Calling it a catastrophe is '''an overstatement'''.}}
##: '''å si''' {{q|obsolete}} — “that is to say”, introducing a qualification.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Jeg kommer gjerne, '''å si''', hvis jeg er frisk.|I'll gladly come, '''that is''', if I am well.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1888|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Fruen fra havet|page=43|passage=jeg har også oplevet dette her. På en måde, at '''sige'''|translation=I have experienced this too. In a way, that is to '''say'''.}}
## To [[recite]], to [[deliver]] orally.
##: {{uxi|nb|Hun '''sa''' et vers utenat.|She '''recited''' a verse from memory.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1872|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Kongs-Emnerne|page=127|passage=Jatgejr skald vil '''sige''' sit kvad til ære for kong Skule|translation=Jatgeir the skald wishes to '''recite''' his poem in honour of King Skule.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1925|author=Sigrid Undset|title=Olav Audunssøn i Hestviken|volume=I|page=182|passage=[hun] '''sa''' eventyr og regler|translation=[She] '''recited''' fairy tales and rhymes.}}
##: '''si fram''', '''si frem''' — “to recite”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|Elevene '''sa fram''' et dikt for klassen.|The pupils '''recited''' a poem to the class.}}
## {{lb|nb|of a text or saying}} To [[say]], to [[read]].
##: {{uxi|nb|Skiltet '''sier''' at veien er stengt.|The sign '''says''' that the road is closed.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1850|author=Bernhard Herre|title=En Jægers Erindringer|page=22|passage=eventyret '''siger''', at denne huldre var fiin og skjær som morgentaagen|translation=The tale '''says''' that this huldra was delicate and fair as the morning mist.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1873|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Kærlighedens komedie|page=94|passage=således '''siger''' jo et gammelt ord|translation=That is what an old saying '''says'''.}}
## {{lb|nb|of an animal}} To [[make]] its characteristic sound.
##: {{uxi|nb|Sauen '''sier''' bæ.|The sheep '''goes''' baa.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnson|title=Bjørnstjerne Bjørnsons fortællinger|page=233|passage=«Hvad '''siger''' katten,» spurte Øyvind|translation=“What does the cat '''say'''?” asked Øyvind.}}
## {{lb|nb|of an object|also impersonal}} To [[make]] a sound; to [[go]].
##: {{uxi|nb|Det '''sa''' klikk da døra gikk igjen.|There '''was''' a click as the door closed.}}
##* {{quote-book|nb|year=1917|author=Knut Hamsun|title=Markens Grøde|volume=II|page=228|passage=klingeling! '''sier''' bjældene langt opi lien|translation=Jingle-jangle! '''go''' the bells far up the hillside.}}
##: '''som sier seks''' {{q|figuratively}} — “that packs a punch; considerable”.
##:: {{uxi|nb|De fikk en regning '''som sa seks'''.|They received a bill '''that really packed a punch'''.}}
# To [[state]], [[assert]], or [[declare]]; to express an [[opinion]].
#: {{uxi|nb|Hva '''sier''' du til forslaget?|What do you '''think''' of the proposal?}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1879|author=Henrik Ibsen|title=Et dukkehjem|page=32|passage=fire tusend otte hundrede kroner. Hvad '''siger''' du til det?|translation=Four thousand eight hundred kroner. What do you '''say''' to that?}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1907|author=Bernt Lie|title=Mot Overmagt|page=242|passage=en fik '''si''' der var sommer, eftersom bjerkekrattet stod grønt|translation=One had to '''say''' it was summer, since the birch scrub was green.}}
#: '''ha noe man skulle ha sagt''' — “to have a say”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|De ansatte bør også '''ha noe de skulle ha sagt'''.|The employees should also '''have a say'''.}}
#: '''man kan si hva man vil''' — “say what you will”.
#:: {{uxi|nb|'''Man kan si hva man vil''', men hun arbeider hardt.|'''Say what you will''', but she works hard.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1880|author=Jonas Lie|title=Rutland|page=204|passage=man '''sige''' nu, hvad man vil!|translation=People may '''say''' what they like!}}
#: '''jeg skal si''' — “I tell you”, emphasizing a statement.
#:: {{uxi|nb|'''Jeg skal si''' det regnet!|It really poured, '''I tell you'''!}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1914|author=Sigrid Undset|title=Vaaren|page=193|passage=aajoda, dama begynder at faa figur, skal jeg '''si'''|translation=Oh yes, the lady is beginning to develop a figure, I '''tell''' you.}}
