=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|nb|si|Si}} commonly introduces direct speech or an {{m|nb|at}} clause. The recipient is normally introduced with {{m|nb|til}}: {{uxi|nb|Hun '''sa''' til meg at hun ville [[komme]].|She '''told''' me that she would come.}}
* The regular present participle is {{m|nb|siende}}. The lexicalized adjective {{m|nb|sigende|t=telling; significant}} preserves the older stem.
* Older quotations may contain ''sige'', ''siger'', ''sagde'' and ''sig'' corresponding to modern ''si'', ''sier'', ''sa'' and imperative ''si''.

