===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|nb|non|síða|t=side}}, from {{inh|nb|gem-pro|*sīdǭ}}, a derivative of {{der|nb|gem-pro|*sīdaz|t=long, hanging down}}. A variant of {{m|nb|side}}.

Compare {{cog|nn|side}}, {{cog|da|side}}, {{cog|sv|sida}}, {{cog|is|síða}}, {{cog|fo|síða}}, {{cog|de|Seite}} and {{cog|en|side|t=side}}.

====Noun====
{{head|nb|noun|g=m|indeclinable}}

# Used in {{l|nb|på si|t=on the side; in addition}}.
#: {{uxi|nb|Hun [[studere|studerer]] og har en [[liten]] [[jobb]] '''på si'''.|She studies and has a small job '''on the side'''.}}
#: {{uxi|nb|Han hadde en [[kjæreste]] '''på si'''.|He had a lover '''on the side'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1952|author=Agnar Mykle|title=«Jeg er like glad», sa gutten|page=43|passage=så var det dét at han hadde ei dame på '''si'''|translation=Then there was the fact that he had a woman on the '''side'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1954|author=Agnar Mykle|title=Lasso rundt fru Luna|page=93|passage=på '''si''', i sin fritid, hadde faren arbeidet med forskjellige ting|translation=On the '''side''', in his spare time, his father had worked on various things.}}

===Etymology 4===
{{wikipedia|lang=no|Solmisasjon}}
[[File:B Note.png|thumb|The note B natural, called ''si'' in fixed-do solmization.]]
{{root|nb|ine-pro|*seh₂k-}}
{{bor+|nb|it|si}}, formed from the initials of {{der|nb|la|[[sanctus|Sāncte]] [[Iohannes|Iohannēs]]|t=Saint John}}, the closing words of the first stanza of the hymn ''[[w:Ut queant laxis|Ut queant laxis]]''.

The first word is the vocative of {{m|la|sānctus|t=holy}}, from {{der|nb|itc-pro|*sanktos}}, a participle of {{m|itc-pro|*sankjō|t=to consecrate}}, ultimately from {{der|nb|ine-pro|*seh₂k-|t=to sanctify}}. The second is a variant of {{m|la|Iōannēs}}, from {{der|nb|grc|Ἰωάννης}}, from {{der|nb|hbo|יוֹחָנָן|tr=Yōḥānān|t=John}}.

Compare {{cog|nn|si}}, {{cog|ca|si}}, {{cog|fr|si}}, {{cog|pt|si}}, {{cog|nl|si}}, {{cog|pl|si}} and {{cog|en|si|t=si, ti}}.

====Noun====
{{head|nb|noun|g=m|definite singular|sien|indefinite plural|sier|definite plural|siene}}

# {{lb|nb|music}} [[#English|si]], [[ti]]; the seventh syllable or scale degree in [[solmization]].
#: {{uxi|nb|Det er en [[halvtone]] fra '''si''' til [[do]].|There is a semitone from '''si''' to do.}}
#* {{quote-book|nb|year=1999|author=Toril Brekke|title=Aske|page=109|passage=det sang i henne … Evinnelige løp. De sang seg selv. Evinnelige uten halvtonen fra '''si''' til do|translation=There was singing inside her … Endless runs. They sang themselves. Endless, without the semitone from '''si''' to do.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In fixed-do solmization, {{m|nb|si}} denotes B natural, called ''h'' in Norwegian letter notation. In movable-do solmization, it denotes the seventh degree of the major scale.

